      "rationale": "This guarded base equation defines sequenceAcc to return the existing accumulator when the loop counter is already above the bound.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-fef3abb92ec888abf14e3bf9a2fd8f282df0e342c4122d6cd092d876bcb85646",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule sequenceAcc(ACC, I, N) => ACC\n    requires I >Int N\n    [concrete, simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "concrete",
        "simplification"
      ],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 22,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "43f49722bb57ff9eafcc5227f4b4353cd12742df4bb56c784efe6e413736cdbf",
      "rationale": "This guarded recurrence defines one concrete sequenceAcc step by appending a space and the decimal rendering of the current counter, incrementing the counter, and recurring.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-43f49722bb57ff9eafcc5227f4b4353cd12742df4bb56c784efe6e413736cdbf",
      "start_line": 14,
      "text": "  rule sequenceAcc(ACC, I, N)\n    => sequenceAcc(\n         seqConcat(\n           seqConcat(ACC, iCons(32, .IntSeq)),\n           strToCodes(Int2String(I))),\n         I +Int 1,\n         N)\n    requires I <=Int N\n    [concrete, simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "simplification"
      ],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 28,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "d55499ddc47bd6adf4d30b16fdbd3314a5db1919e0074fd704e4bfe2e4543f7c",
      "rationale": "This symbolic simplification rule repeats the exact base equation of sequenceAcc so that the defining base case is available during symbolic simplification; it adds no fact beyond that definition.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-d55499ddc47bd6adf4d30b16fdbd3314a5db1919e0074fd704e4bfe2e4543f7c",
      "start_line": 26,
      "text": "  rule sequenceAcc(ACC, I, N) => ACC\n    requires I >Int N\n    [simplification]"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 45,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "02288b5620299a0a1ac5b02b112560d2ffdd21df6457ef2054ea9f3746dbef3b",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines stringSequenceCodes for negative inputs as the empty character-code sequence.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-02288b5620299a0a1ac5b02b112560d2ffdd21df6457ef2054ea9f3746dbef3b",
      "start_line": 44,
      "text": "  rule stringSequenceCodes(N) => .IntSeq\n    requires N <Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 49,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "975c7f6f0a3b75ffe8b642274c4103c08f2594d0bccd1678e974201218b3ab16",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines stringSequenceCodes for nonnegative inputs by seeding the code for zero and invoking the sequenceAcc summary from counter one.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-975c7f6f0a3b75ffe8b642274c4103c08f2594d0bccd1678e974201218b3ab16",
      "start_line": 47,
      "text": "  rule stringSequenceCodes(N)\n    => sequenceAcc(iCons(48, .IntSeq), 1, N)\n    requires N >=Int 0"
    }
